# Build o2-gpu-test for every AliceO2 PR, on the slc10 GPU builder image.
#
# This check lives in the slc10/ directory rather than a slc10-gpu/ one on
# purpose, so the existing slc10 workers pick it up with no new pool: they list
# every *.env in their container's directory, and a check that overrides
# CONTAINER_IMAGE gets its own image without needing its own job.
#
# That works because the ARCHITECTURE is the same. The entrypoint derives it as
# ${CUR_CONTAINER%%-*}_$(uname -m), stripping at the FIRST dash, so slc10 and
# slc10-gpu both mean slc10_x86-64 -- the GPU builder differs in what is
# installed in the image, not in the target platform. Packages are therefore
# interchangeable in principle, and build-one.sh gives each check its own work
# area (mkdir -p "$env_name") in practice, so nothing built under one image is
# reused under the other.
#
# CONTAINER_IMAGE is normally set once per job. Overriding it per check is new;
# no other *.env does it. It works because source_env_files runs after the job's
# environment, and build-loop.sh only ever reads the variable.
CONTAINER_IMAGE=registry.cern.ch/alisw/slc10-gpu-builder:latest

# This check needs GPU hardware, so only workers running in the cluster's "gpu"
# node pool may claim it. claim-builder.sh treats this as a hard filter -- a
# worker elsewhere skips the row rather than taking work it cannot do -- and as a
# sort key, so a GPU worker drains GPU-only rows before work any worker could
# take. Otherwise the scarce machine spends its time on ordinary builds while
# this queue starves.
#
# Nomad's node_pool is a JOB-level field, so serving both pools means two jobs
# sharing this one queue, not one job spanning them. Checks are deliberately not
# split by directory: a GPU worker should still help with ordinary slc10 builds
# when the GPU queue is empty, and being able to is the point of claims.
REQUIRES_POOL=gpu

CI_NAME=build_O2_gpu_test_slc10_x86
CHECK_NAME=build/O2/gpu-test-slc10-x86

# Every O2 PR, not alidist ones: this check exists to catch GPU breakage in O2
# itself. alidist comes along as a development package so a PR is tested against
# the recipes as they are now.
PR_REPO=AliceO2Group/AliceO2
PR_BRANCH=dev
PACKAGE=o2-gpu-test
ALIBUILD_DEFAULTS=o2
DEVEL_PKGS="alisw/alidist master
AliceO2Group/AliceO2 dev O2"

TRUST_COLLABORATORS=true
DONT_USE_COMMENTS=1

# Repeated from o2-alidist.env rather than inherited: *.env files do not inherit
# from each other, only from the DEFAULTS.env chain. If a third slc10 check
# appears, move these two into mesosci/slc10/DEFAULTS.env instead of copying
# them again.
#
# aliBuild 2.0, which is what slc10 is being brought up against, and the CAS
# store, which is the only one carrying slc10_x86-64 packages.
INSTALL_ALIBUILD='alisw/alibuild@refs/pull/1038/head'
REMOTE_STORE=https://s3.cern.ch/swift/v1/alibuild-cas

# BRING-UP: one PR only, because this check CANNOT PASS YET and every attempt
# publishes a red status on somebody's O2 PR.
#
# aliBuild 2.0 starts a detached helper container as
#
#   docker run --detach --entrypoint= <image> sleep inf
#
# and slc10-gpu-builder has no `sleep` on $PATH, so doctor dies with
#
#   exec: "sleep": executable file not found in $PATH
#
# That is a property of the IMAGE plus aliBuild's helper pattern, not of the
# hardware -- it fails identically on a GPU node, so rebuilding will not turn any
# of it green. 31 O2 PRs already carry an "aliBuild doctor error" from this
# check, published while a field-splitting bug let non-GPU workers claim it.
# GitHub cannot delete a status, only supersede it, so those stay red until the
# check can actually pass.
#
# Widen this only once the image ships sleep, or aliBuild uses an absolute
# /bin/sleep (AppleContainerRunner already does: "--entrypoint=/bin/sleep").
# Until then a single PR is enough to tell whether the fix worked, and costs one
# red status instead of dozens.
ONLY_PRS="15692"
